{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-10-27T12:09:22.235Z","author":"pi-agent","author_source":"asserted","agent_harness":"pi","agent_model":"glm-5.3:cloud","agent_model_source":"environment","agent_instance":"204abaf84e89262155a1e246","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"glm-5.3:cloud","source":"environment"},"effort":null,"role":null,"topic":null},"op":"comment_add","patch":[{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-10-27T12:09:22.235Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/comments","value":[{"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:09:22.235Z","author":"pi-agent","text":"Overlap check (re-run 2026-10-27 against pm CLI 2026.10.20 SDK and sibling packages): (a) pm-cli SDK has no parameter/interpolation capability — grep over the installed SDK declarations shows settings mutations are literal audited patches (mutateWorkspaceSettings), templates are literal option maps (loadCreateTemplateOptions/runTemplatesShow), client.create takes literal fields; no 'parameter|interpolat|substitut' matches in templates/workspace-contracts/schema declarations. (b) gh search issues --repo unbraind/pm-cli 'parameter binding'/'preset parameter'/'template parameter': no open upstream work. (c) Fleet sibling scan (src/docs) for parameter-binding/interpolation features: no hits. (d) In-package status: presets accept only a few CLI overrides (--prefix, --force, --dry-run, --replace, --with-seeds) and upgrades of known settings; seed and template values are static literals. Conclusion: no overlap — this adds parameter propagation as an explicit authoring contract while the resolved native fields are still validated by the existing core path (preset validation + the host's audited settings mutation), so no core schema change is required."}]}],"before_hash":"d3a73ee06f1e9f89884b87a1b69fbf1dd2d918e2dee6cd0d5f495f6c42cfd1c8","after_hash":"db924be10ee0a121fa3567524017f4a865537dbf77e867c5a3c8bdec5a928aa9","item_hash_version":3,"event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"a4eed62c773e1c7682f04b53eeefd9da3bc24eff5dace2fb59b680a2cfee6382"}
{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-10-27T14:07:02.393Z","author":"pi-agent","author_source":"asserted","agent_harness":"pi","agent_model":"glm-5.3:cloud","agent_model_source":"environment","agent_instance":"204abaf84e89262155a1e246","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"glm-5.3:cloud","source":"environment"},"effort":null,"role":null,"topic":null},"op":"comment_add","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/comments/1","value":{"created_at":"2026-10-27T14:07:02.392Z","author":"pi-agent","text":"Revert proof (2026-10-27): behaviourally reverted the parameter handling in applyPreset (resolution disabled; raw binding syntax passes through) and re-ran the focused new tests: 8 of 11 fail (one-value-reaches-every-occurrence, default resolution, refusal-before-writes, params-file, diff parity, dry-run, property round-trip, concurrent applies). Restored the implementation: 8/8 params-cli tests pass again. Full suite before the gate: 238 tests pass, 0 fail (node --test --test-concurrency=2 on a saturated 4-core host)."}},{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-10-27T14:07:02.393Z"}],"before_hash":"db924be10ee0a121fa3567524017f4a865537dbf77e867c5a3c8bdec5a928aa9","after_hash":"15c7021e61980ff731e776ddb06520be9cce3f40d76cf7c7deda49ea2b67c946","item_hash_version":3,"event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"dc6c09d3247c8532774debb9b9831ce8706ca96115491ea6520f5e9d2bd9e1a1"}
