{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-10-27T14:56:36.277Z","author":"pi-agent","author_source":"asserted","agent_harness":"pi","agent_model":"glm-5.3:cloud","agent_model_source":"environment","agent_instance":"204abaf84e89262155a1e246","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"glm-5.3:cloud","source":"environment"},"effort":null,"role":null,"topic":null},"op":"comment_add","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/comments/2","value":{"created_at":"2026-10-27T14:56:36.277Z","author":"pi-agent","text":"Real-data validation (2026-10-27), on byte-identical temp copies of this repository's public pm tracker in non-git temp dirs (GIT_CEILING set; the repo tracker itself was never touched): (1) READ-ONLY copy (chmod a-w): parameterized diff with projectKey=acme compared 13 settings leaves -> 1 add, 6 change, id_prefix 'acme-' vs stored 'pm-'; default-resolution diff reported the 'road-' default; supplying an undeclared parameter refused with typed code unknown_parameter listing the declared parameter; a full-file digest proved every tracker byte unchanged afterwards. (2) Writable temp copy: dry-run apply resolved 1 parameter into 3 binding occurrences (id_prefix + two template bodies, all showing acme); an invalid value (uppercase) refused with invalid_value before any write; a real --with-seeds apply read back through the SDK as id_prefix 'acme-', 2/2 template bodies carrying the occurrence, seed item titled 'Define the acme first roadmap initiative', 85 items after seeding (84 tracked items + 1 seed). (3) Note: the audited settings mutation takes a workspace-history lock, so a dry-run apply against the read-only copy refuses with a lock conflict - expected host behavior, mirrored by presets diff which reads without locks."}},{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-10-27T14:56:36.277Z"}],"before_hash":"ae014f15436f8334ad5c63109dc0b31b5bd5b227e8f29985f3ec13b05d94f693","after_hash":"f7553cb56cdb1166b5e6bd9d33bb53b0a0240c25d7cb45991505c78b06273cd6","item_hash_v